H. Which SQL command would you use when:
Creating the schema
Adding a column
Changing column definition
Deleting selected rows
Removing all table rows
Removing the table
Saving a transaction
Undoing a transaction

 IDs                          | INT / BIGINT         
 Money/price                  | DECIMAL(10,2)          
 Names/categories/status      | VARCHAR                
 Date only                    | DATE                   
 Date + time                  | DATETIME / TIMESTAMP 
 Flexible structured metadata | JSON                   

 Requirement                  Command                         
 Create schema/database   | CREATE DATABASE               
 Create table             | CREATE TABLE                  
 Add column               | ALTER TABLE ... ADD COLUMN    
 Change column definition | ALTER TABLE ... MODIFY/CHANGE 
 Delete selected rows     | DELETE ... WHERE              
 Remove all rows          | TRUNCATE TABLE                
 Remove table             | DROP TABLE                    
 Save transaction         | COMMIT                        
 Undo transaction         | ROLLBACK                      

PRIMARY KEY  -> Who is this row?
FOREIGN KEY  -> Which other row is it related to?
UNIQUE       -> No duplicates
NOT NULL     -> Mandatory
CHECK        -> Business rule
DEFAULT      -> Automatic value
DECIMAL      -> Exact money
DATETIME     -> Date + time
JSON         -> Structured flexible data

